# ElevenLabs -- voiceover (Text to Speech scope) AND sound effects (Sound
# Effects scope). The older archcanvas-promo-video used SFX only; this film has
# a voiceover, so the key needs BOTH scopes.
#
# The founder keeps the live key in ../archcanvas/.env.local. scripts/*.mjs read
# this file via `node --env-file=.env`, so copy only the one line across.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=sk_your_key_here

# Voice id for the narration. Chosen from candidates rendered by
# `node --env-file=.env scripts/generate-vo.mjs --audition`.
#
# CHOSEN 2026-09-08: JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb -- "George - Warm, Captivating
# Storyteller", British, male, middle-aged, labelled narrative_story.
#
# Why George over Alice (Xb7hH8MSUJpSbSDYk0k2) and Lily (pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku),
# the other two auditioned, both also British:
#
#   * It is the LOW-REGISTER read, and that is a mix decision as much as a
#     casting one. docs/suno-prompt.md specs a bed that is "deliberately hollow
#     in the middle" -- weighted low and high with 200-2000 Hz left empty for
#     the voice. A low, warm read sits in that gap instead of fighting the
#     bells above it.
#   * It suits the graphite-night opening. The film's first line lands on
#     near-black over near-silence; George is close and unhurried there, where
#     a brighter read would announce.
#   * British, because the product lives on a .uk domain and an American
#     announcer read would make it sound like an ad for something else.
#
# Daniel was NOT auditioned on purpose: the voice library's own label for him
# is "news presenter", and the brief is documentary, not announcer.
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb
